 ### [Hardware Alpha Blending Compositing](5697-hardware-alpha-blending-compositing.md)
-Hardware Alpha Blending Compositing is a technique for direct volume ray casting that leverages the fixed-function or programmable pipeline of a GPU to perform the front-to-back (Over) or back-to-front (Under) compositing equations during rasterization[book]. It solves the problem of accumulating transmittance and color along a ray by mapping the scalar volume data to texture alpha channels and rendering proxy geometry (such as slices or splats) with specific blend factors. It differs from software-based accumulation by offloading the per-sample arithmetic to the hardware blend unit, and from [Back-to-Front Compositing](2078-back-to-front-compositing.md) by relying on the GPU's depth buffer and blend state rather than explicit sorting or shader-based accumulation loops[book].
+Hardware Alpha Blending Compositing is a technique for direct volume ray casting that leverages the fixed-function or programmable pipeline of a GPU to perform the front-to-back (Over) or back-to-front (Under) compositing equations during rasterization. It solves the problem of accumulating transmittance and color along a ray by mapping the scalar volume data to texture alpha channels and rendering proxy geometry (such as slices or splats) with specific blend factors. It differs from software-based accumulation by offloading the per-sample arithmetic to the hardware blend unit, and from [Back-to-Front Compositing](2078-back-to-front-compositing.md) by relying on the GPU's depth buffer and blend state rather than explicit sorting or shader-based accumulation loops.
 
